1
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:42,740
Well, then the moose spun around and slid off the roof.

2
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:45,040
And flew in the back of the car.

3
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:48,260
It knocked out both boxes at the back.

4
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:51,920
And destroyed the C-pillar.

5
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:54,740
-How did it go with you?
Not a scratch.

6
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:57,615
Not even glass splits.

7
00:01:57,620 --> 00:02:00,960
-Why do you buy a car that has rolled 100,000 miles?

8
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:02,240
It's fun.

9
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:05,500
It had not rolled 100,000 miles when I bought it.

10
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:48,380
By then the car had also been to the United States.

11
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:51,420
The plan was to drive the car everywhere on the ground.

12
00:08:51,420 --> 00:08:54,120
But two months ago ...

13
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:56,300
I drove on an icy road.

14
00:08:56,300 --> 00:08:59,980
The car started to gossip and I drove too fast.

15
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:03,200
I drove into a tree at 80 km/h and everything broke on the car.

16
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:06,420
Even the crankshaft in the engine broke.

17
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:09,360
There was nothing to save on the car.

18
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:13,640
I felt bad because all the plans I had were now gone.

19
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:41,140
It will be fun to be able to travel in a car again.

20
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:46,360
The year 2020 will drive this car all the way from the Netherlands to Japan.

21
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:51,640
Drive the car back to the Subaru factory where it was manufactured.

22
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:55,500
I'm pretty sure we can drive all the way without any problems.

23
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:57,660
-It will cost a fortune?

24
00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:02,840
Yes, but I hope I can find some sponsors.

25
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:07,180
That people can help pay for gasoline.

26
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:10,260
-What is the plan when you arrive at Japan.
Will you drive the car home?

27
00:10:10,260 --> 00:10:12,720
If Subaru wants the car, they have to take it.

28
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:07,400
-You seem to like the car.
Absolutely, I love it.

29
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,880
I have big plans.

30
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:14,540
I will foil large parts of the car.

31
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:18,040
All stories with the car, even small details like the scratches here at the back.

32
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:21,200
All scratches have their own history.

33
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:24,020
It should be foiled but the history of the car.

34
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:28,180
On the bonnet I will put a new map just like the old car.

35
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:32,180
Who will show the entire trip from the Netherlands to Japan.

36
00:11:32,180 --> 00:11:38,980
Text about the plans for this car and that we drive a Subaru with 1 million km on the meter.

37
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:44,680
That's why the website is called so.

38
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:47,860
On the Facebook page "Sunglobe - Team Legacy".

39
00:13:47,860 --> 00:13:50,360
Can you follow all trips.

40
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:54,400
The goal is to drive to Japan.

41
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:57,000
And show the world ..

42
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,380
... that everyone has to buy a Subaru.

43
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:02,400
-It was very nice to meet and have a lovely trip home.

44
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:03,760
Thanks so much.

45
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:06,680
Bye!
